    SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-Element-Commercial.

    PlayerView with surface_type="texture_view" so the video pixels live in a
    regular hardware-accelerated View instead of SurfaceView's separately-
    composited hardware surface. SurfaceView's surface lags / glitches when
    the parent Compose layout applies transforms (Modifier.offset, scale,
    movableContentOf) — that's what caused the video to visibly shift when
    the user dragged the in-app mini player or returned to fullscreen.
    TextureView is slightly more expensive per frame (one extra GPU copy)
    but stays glued to the Compose layout exactly, which is what we need
    for the floating mini player and the fullscreen<->mini transitions.

    `use_controller=false` because we draw our own Compose controller bar
    over the top of this view.
-->
<androidx.media3.ui.PlayerView
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    app:surface_type="texture_view"
    app:use_controller="false" />
